  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef baked a full tray of donuts, but couldn't resist and ate them all!\n\nThe tray had XXX donuts, and each donut contains YYY calories.\n\nHow many calories did Chef consume in total?\n\n\nInput Format\nThe only line of input contains two space-separated integers XXX and YYY - the number of donuts and the calorie count of each one.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint a single integer: the total number of calories consumed by Chef.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X≤101 \\leq X \\leq 101≤X≤10",
      "200≤Y≤300200 \\leq Y \\leq 300200≤Y≤300"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 280",
        "output": "560",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef ate two donuts, each containing 280280280 calories. The total number of calories is thus 280+280=560280 + 280 = 560280+280=560."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6 237",
        "output": "1422",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef ate six donuts, each containing 237237237 calories. The total number of calories is thus 6⋅237=14226\\cdot 237 = 14226⋅237=1422."
      }
    ]
  },
